  "observations": [
    "TCNI0028/profile28 binds one exact Byte/Int16/Int64/Single/Double/legacy DateTime descriptor to zero or multiple original requests. All-NULL and empty groups still require actual source metadata agreement; singleton TCNI21 and LONG/Currency original families remain separate.",
    "Producer and independent proof retain full source/program/constraint/index/declaration checks and separate complete AFTER reconstruction. IEEE bit-sensitive values, exact Int64 beyond Double precision, forwarded records, historical materialization, cancellation and protected companions are exercised.",
    "Private dispatch wrappers cannot erase descriptor metadata before borrowed native request construction. Immutable data-grammar agreement is checked at terminal reconstruction; legacy profiles that deliberately share one grammar retain that existing policy. Forged old wrappers and checked reverse conversion refuse before effects, including fresh V3 recovery.",
    "Single-local-table GROUP BY/HAVING and aggregate/computed ordering use complete existing query staging. Direct Text/Decimal fields preserve actual native declarations; fixed computed/parameter outputs use static query declarations including empty results. No type or width is inferred from result rows.",
    "NULL groups, COUNT(*) versus COUNT(field), explicit declared inputs, empty global COUNT, aggregate ordering and late/TOP-omitted eager errors are covered. The current uncast COUNT Int64 descriptor is an implementation observation, not a native Access metadata equivalence claim.",
    "Existing consuming review/No/Yes/save/acknowledgment/reopen services publish one complete native image with actual matched/changed counts. Exact BIGINT prompts, prior-result preservation, stale capabilities and complete raw AFTER are observed through headless Desktop journeys."
  ],
